{"dog":{"age_group":"senior","application_url":"https://www.nycacc.org/adopt/adoption-process/","availability_detail":"available","breed_display":"Medium mixed breed","breed_primary":"Medium Mixed Breed Cross","description_text":"Since I'm a long stay pup, my adoption fee has been reduced! Visit me today to find out my favorite treats and how you can take me home!\n\nDarla arrived at MACC as a stray with no known history. Darla has been observed to be highly fearful while in care, noted to balk and thrash on leash when handlers attempt to return her to kennel. Due to the high level of fear, stress, and anxiety, we recommend an experienced adult only home.\n\nI love to be loved, but on my own terms! Let's brush up on some canine body language together!\n\nA Volunteer Wrote: They don't get easier or sweeter than Darla, who is so happy to amble along to the park and just sniff the air, the grass, the world outside of her pop up crate. This girl is so gentle and kind, and she's so happy to get out of her pop up crate in the middle of a noisy hallway; her fans are desperate for her to be lying next to a loving person on a couch somewhere, and not here! Please come meet this gentle girl and consider making her a part of your family.","detail_url":"https://nycaccpets.shelterbuddy.com/animal/animalDetails.asp?s=adoption&searchTypeId=4&animalType=3%2C16&pagesize=75&task=view&tpage=13&searchType=4&animalid=202799","id":"6f6f666e1996d1b4365cff3bd55cecc4","image_urls":["https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/image/bace69cfd2554d00858347cc53c99736-1787048665-1787054699-jpeg/600---n","https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/image/4102c8e9ceae4ab0a7c036e43bc157bb-1787048665-1787048665-jpeg/600---n","https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/image/94db9ffb77434206a620562ea76a5515-1785704370-1785704384-jpeg/600---n","https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/image/4986704681734e7d9810899e253ab979-1785704370-1785704370-jpeg/600---n","https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/image/a97c043